  kept first, then the rest in document order while they fit; the fold ends with a note that LISTS the omitted
  headings. Fenced code never splits. Prose without `##` sections (or nothing fitting) falls back to the ADR-0169 head
  cut. Caps unchanged; under-cap files byte-identical. Canonical probe on the REAL 14o workspace, local AND on zc-01
  (fold md5 30d95dcfdd72 on both): 8,062-char fold, 20 of 25 sections kept INCLUDING "## Naming (MANDATORY)"; omitted:
  Feature flags; Observability; Internationalization; Concurrency; Performance. 14u and 13 unchanged (under cap, no
  note). Gates: ruff/mypy clean; full suite 3923 passed (5 new tests: mandate section past the cap kept whole and in
  order; prose fallback with the counted note; fence safety; determinism; no-section-fits fallback).

